    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 288\n\nTO THE SENATE:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nSenate Bill Number 7161, entitled:\n\n    \"AN ACT to amend the elder law, in relation to rules and regulations\n      pertaining to the operation of social adult day care programs\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This bill would require the New York State Office for the Aging (NYSO-\nFA) to regulate all Social Adult Day Services (SADS) programs statewide,\nregardless  of  their  source  of  funding  or whether they are run by a\npublic or private entity.\n\n  I continue to support the need for uniform, consistent  standards  for\nregulating  SADS  program providers. However, this bill suffers from the\nsame fundamental flaw as the bill I vetoed last  year  --  it  does  not\nidentify  a designated source of funds to offset the significant cost of\nimplementing an entirely new regulatory system for the hundreds of  SADS\nprograms  that operate statewide. Such funding decisions should occur in\nthe context of the annual budget negotiations, and for this reason, I am\ntherefore constrained to veto this bill.\n\n  Last year, I instructed NYSOFA, the Department of  Health  (DOH),  and\nOffice  of the Medicaid Inspector General (OMIG) to work with stakehold-\ners to begin developing a regulatory framework that balances  the  needs\nof  all  SADS recipients with the State's fiscal concerns. Those efforts\nare on-going. To date, SADS programs that are being funded  directly  by\nNYSOFA or through its local government partners are being assessed annu-\nally  to  determine  their  compliance with existing NYSOFA regulations.\nMoreover, DOH has issued extensive guidance to managed  long  term  care\n(MLTC)  plans  that contract with SADS providers to ensure that all SADS\nproviders meet the standards and requirements of NYSOFA  regulations.  I\nam  directing  these  agencies  to  continue  their efforts to develop a\nfiscally-sound statewide solution that  aligns  with  the  policy  goals\nadvanced by this bill.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
